content_copy
expand_less
NEXT_PUBLIC_API_URL=http://localhost:4000

Run npm install to install dependencies.

Run npm run dev to start the frontend development server.

Action:

Open your browser to http://localhost:3000 (or whatever URL Next.js provides).

You can now test the full workflow locally. The frontend will make calls to your locally running Go backend.

Cloud Deployment:

Deploy your backend using the encore deploy command, targeting your chosen cloud provider. Encore will give you a permanent public API URL.

Deploy your frontend to Vercel or Netlify. In the project's environment variable settings, set NEXT_PUBLIC_API_URL to your permanent public Encore URL.
